// rustc borrowck/issue-58776-borrowck-scans-children.rs — upstream E0506
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: admit · root bck.NEW-CAPLOAN — RE-PORTED AS-IS 2026-09-07 (stage 4)
// ── BUCKET 2: re-ported as-is, still admitted, still a defect. The old port had
//    substituted `i64` for `String`; with upstream's `String` (so the assignment is a
//    real replace of an owning local, not a scalar store) it is still admitted.
// ── ROOT RE-CHECKED, and it is sharper than bck.C. The loan is not lost because the
//    closure is opaque — a loan minted AND used inside one closure body IS tracked
//    ("cannot assign to 'g' because it is borrowed", measured 2026-09-07). What is lost
//    is a loan that CROSSES the boundary. MEASURED ONE-VARIABLE PAIR, only the minting
//    callee differs:
//      let r: &i64 = id(&g);            via `fn id(x:&i64)->&i64`  -> REFUSED
//         "cannot assign to 'g' because it is borrowed"
//      let r: &i64 = (|| { &g })();     via an immediately-invoked closure -> ADMITS
//    Same root, second door: a capture that MUTABLY borrows an upvar also deposits no
//    loan — see mut-borrow-conflict-in-closures-vec--bounded, whose pair is the same
//    program with `&mut y` written directly (REFUSED) instead of captured (ADMITS).
// Original path: tests/ui/borrowck/issue-58776-borrowck-scans-children.rs
// upstream commit: 4b0c9d76ae7d387229caea55cfa73c280b08b8a7
// upstream construct: lines 2-7 —
//     let mut greeting = "Hello world!".to_string();
//     let res = (|| (|| &greeting)())();
//     greeting = "DEALLOCATED".to_string();   //~^ ERROR cannot assign
//     drop(greeting);
// Modifications:
//   · `"...".to_string()` -> `String::from("...")` (logos.mem.string spelling)
//   · `drop(greeting)` is dropped: Logos drops at scope exit and the upstream `drop` is
//     only there to make the assignment's target definitely dead. `res` is still USED
//     afterwards, which is what keeps the loan live.
//   · assert -> exit code: `fn main() -> i32`
package issue_58776_borrowck_scans_children;
use logos.mem.string;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut greeting = String::from("Hello world!");
    let res: &String = (|| { return (|| { return &greeting; })(); })();
    greeting = String::from("DEALLOCATED");
    return res.len() as i32;
}
